  "notes": {
    "base": "New base: arm A is upstream dev 62eaa9dc249b67567b9cbc83e43fbc875a8b94c1 ('Merge pull request #2142 from JustVugg/docs/coffee-line'); the 2026-10-15 manifests (../final/pr1) used dev 7b55a9b3792527f52d1a2337fd9e312b9a7983e3. The pr1 tip 7e9d2d20816398c25dc979e952ce924cc1012fc3 (rb/pr1/reap-prefill, tree 2de8c223fc1188ce5c60d628028af704184395a0) is 21 commits on top of this base (meta/tips.txt: dev_is_ancestor_of_pr1=yes). dev still refuses the batched GPU MoE for the 132-expert model: every A serve.log has 'v4_gpu moe-batch=off (unsupported model geometry)', every B/C serve.log 'v4_gpu moe-batch=on bank=132-experts', and only C 'v4_gpu moe-double=on'.",
    "prewarm": "Expert-cache prewarm: the base includes upstream #2111 (463f8443, 'a serve fills the expert cache before its first request (#2109)'), so both dev and the pr1 tip prewarm at serve start. At --ram 40 the plan holds 59 of 132 experts per layer, so the prewarm picks experts from .coli_usage, which was empty (size 0, same mtime) before and after every sample (sample.txt usage_before/usage_after; summary.json usage_history_changed []). Every A/B/C serve.log says '[v4] expert cache: 59 of 132 experts per layer fit and no usage history says which, so it fills as experts are used': the prewarm read nothing, and the expert cache started empty in every sample as on 2026-10-15.",
    "cache_state": "The OS page cache was not dropped between samples. The run began with one discarded warm-up sample W (seq 1, a separate server process on the pr1 tip, both requests; texts identical to the reference) before A s1. Unlike the 2026-10-15 run, no host journal was captured for this window, so the serve unit's memory peak (used then to show round 1 was partly cold) is not available and the cache state per sample cannot be stated from evidence. Observed: A request-1 TTFT s1 129.337 s vs s2/s3 128.915/128.762 s (s1 0.39% slower than the s2/s3 mean); medians are over all 3 samples. Run order (seq 2-10): A s1 B s1 C s1 B s2 C s2 A s2 C s3 A s3 B s3.",
    "variability": "TTFT stdev / CV over 3 samples, every arm and request: A r1 0.298 s / 0.23%, A r2 0.585 s / 0.29%, B r1 0.172 s / 0.23%, B r2 0.180 s / 0.16%, C r1 0.073 s / 0.11%, C r2 0.012 s / 0.01%; the largest prompt tok/s CV is 0.29%.",
